systematically wrong. A

116
00:07:30,860 --> 00:07:34,019
causal model is the system's internal
understanding of which

117
00:07:34,019 --> 00:07:37,899
actions cause which outcomes. This is
related to but

118
00:07:37,899 --> 00:07:41,139
distinct from a world model. While a world
model

119
00:07:41,139 --> 00:07:44,459
predicts what will happen next, a causal
model explains

120
00:07:44,920 --> 00:07:48,319
why things happen. When an agent learns
moving right

121
00:07:48,319 --> 00:07:51,600
causes reward, it has developed a
different causal model

122
00:07:51,600 --> 00:07:54,759
than the true structure where coin
collection causes reward.

123
00:07:55,399 --> 00:08:00,600
The training environment supports both
true causal structure Action

